  "id": "uffizi",
  "name": "Galleria degli Uffizi",
  "city": "Florence",
  "subtitle": "The east corridor",
  "blurb": "A long flat-ceilinged corridor under grotesque frescoes and dark crossbeams, daylight down one whole side, a checkerboard marble floor and a line of empty plinths.",
  "corridorNote": "Modelled on the east corridor of the Uffizi: a flat coffered ceiling divided by heavy dark wooden crossbeams with symmetrical grotesque frescoes painted between them in gold, red and muted blue on cream; a continuous frieze of small dark-framed portraits running above the picture rail; off-white plaster on the inner wall carrying large gold-framed paintings; a run of tall rectangular windows down the outer wall flooding the hall with daylight; classical statuary on dark squared plinths down both sides behind brass stanchions and red velvet rope; and a highly polished diagonal checkerboard floor of dark charcoal and pale grey marble that reflects the light from the windows in long streaks.",
